cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use iQuantize in your research or publish models made with it, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "iQuantize: A Desktop Workspace for Quantizing Large Language Models to GGUF, MLX and ONNX"
abstract: >-
  iQuantize is a cross-platform desktop application for quantizing large
  language models to the GGUF, MLX and ONNX formats. It recommends
  quantization settings for a target device, shows each tensor being
  quantized, measures the result against the original model (perplexity,
  KL divergence, top-1 agreement, prompt suites and speed), and generates
  model cards whose numbers come from those measurements.
authors:
  - name: iQuantize contributors
    website: "https://github.com/Fazmin/iQuantize/blob/main/CONTRIBUTORS.md"
version: 0.2.22
date-released: 2026-10-29
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Fazmin/iQuantize"
url: "https://github.com/Fazmin/iQuantize"
keywords:
  - quantization
  - large language models
  - GGUF
  - llama.cpp
  - MLX
  - ONNX Runtime
  - model compression
  - Hugging Face
